{"Title":"An Act making corrective changes to certain general and special laws","BillNumber":"S3019","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"S29","Name":"Senate Committee on Rules","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S29","ResponseDate":"2024-12-30T22:22:02.94"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S3019/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Amendment","Pinslip":"Senate, December 30, 2024 - The committee on Rules to whom was referred House Bill relative to individuals with intellectual or developmental disabilities (House, No. 4396); reports, recommending that the same ought to pass with an amendment striking out all after the enacting clause and inserting in place thereof the text of Senate document numbered 3019; and by striking out the title and inserting in place thereof the following title: \"An Act making corrective changes to certain general and special laws\".","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 3 of the General Laws is hereby amended by adding the following section:- \r\n\tSection 76. (a) There shall be a law revision commission which shall consist of: the chairs of the joint committee on the judiciary or their designees, who shall serve as co-chairs; the attorney general or a designee; 4 attorneys admitted to practice law in the commonwealth, 1 of whom shall be appointed by the president of the senate, 1 of whom shall be appointed by the speaker of the house of representatives, 1 of whom shall be appointed by the minority leader of the senate and 1 of whom shall be appointed by the minority leader of the house of representatives; 1 person to be appointed by the Massachusetts District Attorneys Association; 1 person to be appointed by the committee for public counsel services; and 3 persons to be appointed by the governor, 1 of whom shall be a retired judge, 1 of whom shall be a faculty member of an accredited law school in the commonwealth and 1 of whom shall be a historian with expertise in the laws of the commonwealth.\r\n\t(b) The appointed members of the commission shall serve staggered 4-year terms. Vacancies in the membership of the commission shall be filled by the original appointing authority for the remainder of the unexpired term \r\n\t(c) The commission shall: (i) examine common law, general and special laws of the commonwealth and judicial decisions to identify defects and anachronisms in the wording of certain laws and recommend any necessary reforms; (ii) receive and consider proposed amendments to such laws as recommended by the American Law Institute, the National Conference of Commissioners on Uniform State Laws, bar associations and any other learned bodies; (iii) receive and consider proposed changes to any language from judges, justices, public officials, lawyers and the public; (iv) recommend changes in the law to modify or eliminate antiquated and inequitable rules of law and to bring the law into harmony with modern conditions; (v) recommend the express repeal of statutes repealed by implication or held unconstitutional by a state or federal court; (vi) evaluate and make recommendations on the consolidation of session laws into the General Laws; and (vii) make recommendations to improve the openness and accessibility of state laws, including the use of open-source software tools. \r\n\t(d)  Counsel to the senate and counsel to the house of representatives shall jointly provide such personnel as may be necessary to coordinate the activities of the commission and assist the commission in drafting legislative proposals as requested. \r\n\t(e) The commission shall meet at least 4 times annually. At the close of each regular session of the general court, the commission shall submit a report of its findings and recommendations, including drafts of proposed legislation necessary to implement those recommendations, to the clerks of the senate and the house of representatives, the house and senate committees on ways and means and the joint committee on the judiciary. \r\n\t SECTION 2  Section 15F of chapter 6 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2022 Official Edition, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 2 and 3, the words “Employ Handicapped Persons Week” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- Persons with Disabilities Employment Week.  \r\n\tSECTION 3. Section 15LLLL of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 2, the word “Autistic” and inserting in place thereof the following word:- Autism.  \r\n\tSECTION 4. Section 15OOOOO of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 5, the words “disabled individuals” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- individuals with disabilities.    \r\n\tSECTION 5. Section 40 of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 4 and 5, the words “disabled American veterans” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- American veterans with disabilities. \r\n\tSECTION 6. Section 56 of said chapter 6 is hereby amended by striking out, in line 48, as so appearing, the words “and handicapped persons” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- persons and persons with disabilities.  \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\r\n\tSECTION 7. Section 106 of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 11, the words “who are disabled” and inserting in place thereof the following words:-  with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 8. Section 131A of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 3, the words “the aged and disabled” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- aged persons and persons with disabilities.   \r\n\tSECTION 9. Section 131B of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 10 and 11, the words “the aged and disabled” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- aged persons and persons with disabilities.   \r\n\tSECTION 10. Section 143 of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 11, the words “handicapped persons” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- persons with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 11. Section 172 of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 92 and 93, the words “disabled person” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- person with a disability.   \r\n\tSECTION 12. Section 172C of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out the definition of “Disabled person” and inserting in place thereof the following definition:- \r\n\t“Person with a disability”, a person with an intellectual or a developmental disability as defined in section 1 of chapter 123B or who otherwise has an intellectual, developmental or physical disability and who, as a result of such intellectual, developmental or physical disability, is wholly or partially dependent on others to meet the daily living needs of such person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 13. Said section 172C of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in lines 16 and 17, the words “disabled person” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 14. Said section 172C of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 18, the words “elderly or disabled persons” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- elderly persons or persons with disabilities.   \r\n\tSECTION 15. Said section 172C of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in lines 20 and 21, the words “disabled persons” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- persons with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 16. Said section 172C of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in lines 33 and 34, the words “elderly or disabled person” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- elderly person or person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 17. Said section 172C of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 36, the words “the disabled” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- persons with disabilities.  \r\n\tS\tSECTION 18. Section 172E of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 10, the words “or disabled person” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- person or person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 19. Said section 172E of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 13, the words “or disabled persons” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- person or person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 20. Said section 172E of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 21, the words “the disabled” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- persons with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 21. Section 178C of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 60, and in lines 138 and 139, the words “mentally retarded person” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- person with an intellectual or a developmental disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 22. Section 178K of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 236, the words “the mentally retarded” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- a person with an intellectual  or developmental disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 23. Said section 178K of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 259, the words “mentally retarded person” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- person with an intellectual or a developmental disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 24. Section 191 of said chapter 6, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 17, the words “handicapping conditions” and inserting in place thereof the following word:- disabilities.   \r\n\tSECTION 25. Section 16D of chapter 6A of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 58 and 59, the words “the disabled and chronically ill” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- persons with disabilities and persons who are chronically ill.   \r\n\tSECTION 26. Section 16R of said chapter 6A, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 5, the words “is disabled” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- has a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 27. Section 18B of said chapter 6A, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 153, the word “disabled” and inserting in place thereof the following word:- disability.   \r\n\tSECTION 28. Section 2 of chapter 6C of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 84 and in lines 87 and 88, the words “a disabled rider advocate” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- an advocate for riders with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 29. Section 5 of chapter 6D of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 13, the words “in racial, ethnic and disabled communities” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- by race, ethnicity and disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 30. Section 4H of chapter 7 of the General Laws, as appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 84, and in lines 87 and 88, the words “disabled persons protection commission” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- commission for the protection of persons with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 31. Section 22N of said chapter 7 is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 13 and 14, as so appearing, the words “mental retardation” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- intellectual or a developmental disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 32. Section 50 of said chapter 7, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 34 and 35, and in line 37, the words “or disabled workers” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- workers or workers with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 33. Section 27 of chapter 7C of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 13, the word “handicapped” and inserting in place thereof the following word:- disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 34. Section 9 of chapter 8 of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 30, the word “handicapped” and inserting in place thereof the following word:- disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 35. Section 38 of chapter 10 of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 9, the words “retarded children” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- children with intellectual or a developmental disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 36. Said section 38 of said chapter 10, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 133, the words “handicapped person” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- person with a disability.   \r\n\tSECTION 37. Section 15B of chapter 15 of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 4, the words “visually-handicapped children” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- children with visual impairments.  \r\n\tSECTION 38. Section 13 of chapter 15D of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 48 and 49, the words “disabled parents than to the children of non-disabled parents” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- parents with disabilities than to the children of parents without disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 39. Section 2 of chapter 18 of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 86, the word “disabled” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 40. Said section 2 of said chapter 18, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 179, the words “adult handicapped” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- adults with disabilities. \r\n\t  \tSECTION 41. Section 5 of said chapter 18, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 18, the words “the disabled and the handicapped resident” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- and residents with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 42. Section 21 of chapter 19 of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by inserting after the word “of”, in lines 10 and 15, each time it appears, the following words:- persons who are. \r\n\tSECTION 43. Said section 21 of said chapter 19, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by inserting after the word “intellectual”, in lines 11, 18 and 32, each time it appears, the following words:- or developmental.   \r\n\tSECTION 44. Said section 21 of said chapter 19, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 16, the words “and mentally retarded individuals” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- persons and persons with intellectual or developmental disabilities.    \r\n\tSECTION 45. Said section 4 of said chapter 19A, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out the second paragraph and inserting in place thereof the following paragraph:-  \r\n\tThe department shall also serve as an advocate for the needs of adults with disabilities as such needs and services overlap with the needs and services of  elderly persons.  \r\n\tSECTION 46. Section 40 of said chapter 19A, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 47, the words “disabled enrollees’” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- enrollees with disabilities.   \r\n\tSECTION 47. Said section 40 of said chapter 19A, as so appearing, is hereby s further amended by striking out, in lines 49 and 50, the words “disabled individuals” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- individuals with disabilities.   \r\n\tSECTION 48. Section 7 of chapter 19B of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 2, the words:- mental retardation.  \r\n\tSECTION 49. Section 8 of said chapter 19B, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 3, the words:- mental retardation.  \r\n\tSECTION 50. Said section 8 of said chapter 19B, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in lines 6 and 7, the words “the mentally retarded” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- persons with intellectual or developmental disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 51. Section 19 of said chapter 19B, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 126, 139, 280 and 281, 305, 384, 390 and 391, and 394 and 395, the words “disabled persons protection commission” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- commission for the protection of persons with disabilities. \r\n\tSECTION 52. Chapter 19C of the General Laws is hereby amended by striking out the title and inserting in place thereof the following title:- \r\n\tCOMMISSION FOR THE PROTECTION OF PERSONS WITH DISABILITIES.\r\n\tSECTION 53. Section 1 of said chapter 19C, as appearing in the 2022 Official Edition, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 4 and 33, the words “disabled person” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- person with a disability.   \r\n\tSECTION 54. Said section 1 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out the definition of “Caretaker” and inserting in place thereof the following definition:- \r\n\t''Caretaker'', a parent, guardian or other person or agency responsible for the health or welfare of a person with a disability, whether in the same home as the person with a disability or in a relative's home, a foster home or any other day or residential setting.  \r\n\tSECTION 55. Said section 1 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 13, the words “disabled persons protection commission” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- commission for the protection of persons with disabilities. \r\n\tSECTION 56. Said section 1 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out the definition of “Disabled person”.  \r\n\tSECTION 57. Said section 1 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in lines 17 and 18, the words “is otherwise mentally or physically disabled” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- otherwise has an intellectual, developmental or physical disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 58. Said section 1 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in lines 31 and 32, 42 and 46, the words “disabled persons” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- persons with disabilities.   \r\n\tSECTION 59. Said section 1 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by inserting after the definition of “Mandated reporter” the definition:- \r\n\t“Person with a disability”, a person between the ages of 18 to 59, inclusive, who is a person with an intellectual or a developmental disability as defined in section 1 of chapter 123B or who otherwise has an intellectual, developmental or physical disability and, as a result of such disability, is wholly or partially dependent on others to meet daily living needs.\r\n\tSECTION 60. Said section 1 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in lines 39 and 41, the words “disabled person or persons” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- person or persons with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 61. Section 2 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 2, the first time they appear, and in line 5, the words “disabled persons” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- persons with disabilities.   \r\n\tSECTION 62. Said section 2 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in lines 2 and 3, the words “, to be known as the disabled persons protection commission”. \r\n\tSECTION 63. Section 3 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 20 and 21, and in lines 28 and 29, the words “disabled persons” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- persons with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 64. Section 4 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 1, 11, 16, 26, 28 and 35, the words “disabled person” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 65. Said section 4 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 29, the words “disability or otherwise mentally disabled” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- or developmental disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 66. Said section 4 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in lines 30 and 31, the words “disabled person is physically disabled” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- person with a disability is a person with a physical disability   \r\n\tSECTION 67. Section 5 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 1, 13, 33, 50, 63, 73 and 75, and in lines 77 and 78, the words “disabled person” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 68. Said section 5 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 9, the words “disabled person’s health” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- person with a disability’s health.   \r\n\tSECTION 69. Said section 5 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 12, the words “disabled person’s residence” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- person with a disability’s residence.   \r\n\tSECTION 70. Section 6 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 10 and 15, the words “disabled person” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 71. Section 7 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 4, 6 and 7, 12, 13, 16, 17 and 18, 18, 20 and 21, 22, 29, 35, 39 and 40, 46, 47 and 48, 59, 61, 65, 67 and 68, the words “disabled person” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words: - person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 72. Section 8 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 2, the words “disabled person” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- person with a disability.   \r\n\tSECTION 73. Said section 8 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 6, the words “disabled persons” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- the person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 74. Section 10 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 7, 13, 19 and 29, the words “disabled person” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 75. Section 11 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in line 9, the words “disabled person” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- person with a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 76. Section 13 of said chapter 19C, as so appearing, is hereby amended by striking out, in lines 1 and 8, the words “disabl