such person to maintain decent, safe and sanitary housing and who has been determined, pursuant to regulations issued by the secretary of housing and livable communities, to have an impairment which is expected to be of long, continued and indefinite duration, which substantially impedes the ability to live independently in conventional housing and which is of such a nature that such ability could be improved by more suitable housing conditions; provided, however, that except as required by federal law and notwithstanding any other law to the contrary, a history of alcohol or substance use shall not constitute a qualifying impairment; provided further, that eligibility for protection as a person with a disability under state or federal anti-discrimination laws shall not constitute a guarantee of eligibility for housing as a person with a disability of low income; and provided further, that a person who has a disability as defined in paragraph 17 of section 1 of chapter 151B shall still meet the definition  herein in order to be eligible for housing as a person with a disability of low income.  \r\n\tSECTION 232. Section 26 of said chapter 121B is hereby amended by striking out, in line 175, and in lines 182 and 183, as so appearing, the words “handicapped persons” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- persons with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 233. Said section 26 of said chapter 121B is hereby further amended by striking out, in line 176, as so appearing, the words “is handicapped” and inserting in place thereof the following words:- has a disability.  \r\n\tSECTION 234. Said section 26 of said chapter 121B is hereby further amended by striking out, in lines 184 and 186, as so appearing, the words “handicapped residents” and inserting in place thereof, in each instance, the following words:- residents with disabilities.  \r\n\tSECTION 235. Said section 26 of said chapter 121B is hereby further amended by striking out, in lines 262 a